[Music]  the division 2 is officially out very  exciting for fans of the original one  including myself I've been waiting for  this game for a long time we have  already been playing it for a few days  Eddie because we started it when the  early access got underway a few days ago  I think one of the biggest questions of  this game which I totally empathize with  being a person who doesn't tend to play  multiplayer games is is this game fun so  like if you're getting into it if you  don't already have a friendship group  who's super into the series if you're  not a fan of playing The Strangers is it  still a fun game to play on your own  absolutely it is but there's like  there's a lot that we can talk about  this but yeah my main takeaway after  playing this game for the past few days  for like 15-20 hours so far is that you  can absolutely have a good time playing  by yourself it might not always be the  ideal way to play or it might not be for  everybody but I personally have had a  really good time playing by myself the  main thing that gets me thinking about  whether or not I should all want to is  that the division 2 is so good with  matchmaking you because I definitely  know what it feels like to not always  have friends who want to play on my game  of choice all my platform of choice  which is usually PC and the division 2  is just fantastic at matchmaking you  into whatever it is you want to do and  that's especially with the addition of  the coal for backup button which you can  pop into your menu and select at any  point and someone can just answer the  call and just hop along to help you with  whatever it is you happen to be doing  and I find it really enjoyable and one  of the things I really love about  playing with other people is if I do  something silly if I go in gung-ho and  get myself killed that's not the be-all  and end-all I don't have to think about  where my closest respawn point is  although I will say one of the things  that's always popping off at games like  MMOs and stuff that I tried out is that  I quite like to be the hero of these  kinds of games and you lose that a  little bit when you're part of a group  but you get you really get it back again  when you're playing solo yeah you  absolutely do like so the thing I love  about playing solo it's not that I don't  like playing a multiplayer but  you know when you're playing solo like I  like to do things at my own pace on my  own terms it's just like what you said  you know when you're you know thinking  about a situation like where are you  gonna flank from what's the position  you're gonna take what's the angle  you're gonna take when you have a bunch  of random people while it might help you  overall sometimes they can be kind of  detracting force if you guys are not  unified and and also at the same time  like I like to have a plan I go in with  my plan and I execute it and yeah it  might be like a little bit more  challenging by yourself but like that  sense of fulfillment and reward like  when you finish and you're gonna knock  down a yellow enemy you know all by  yourself I think that feels really  really good it really does and there is  a random element and which some people  are a huge fan of I know generally I am  I don't really mind the kinds of people  I'm being matched with whether they're  people who want to open every single bag  like I do or whether they're people who  just want to go gung-ho and run I tend  toward fitting into whatever play style  the the people or person I'm with  decides they want to go with we're just  fine but it is really nice because this  world is it's beautiful the levels are  really interesting they're really  intricate arenas and being able to pace  them out as you say on your own  strategize and it's it's all up to you  it's a traveling on your own it's just  kind of an exciting experience to have  without just feeling like you need to go  along with what the people who are in  your team are doing I think the other  element here is like when you get into a  clan so you can still play solo but your  achievements you know get routed back  into your clans overall achievements you  can have that solo experience but also  contribute to something more meaningful  look personally I'm because I hate  respawning at random locations so much I  am the kind of person who will match  make for anything I do whether it's free  roam whether it's a side mission whether  it's a control point but there is a very  particular joy in doing these things on  your own that I really believe you don't  get as much in the multiplayer despite  how great the multiplayer is it's  something that Michael Higham said in in  his pay  on the how fun the game is in single  player on GameSpot and I think it's  definitely worth trying both to be  honest I think they both have their  place and it's great that the game  supports both as well as it does yeah I  mean I think that's my favorite part  about the game too is that while my own  personal preference might be to play  solo in no way does the game ever push  you down one or the other path it does  some things to encourage you to play  with other people there's no penalties  for not apart from maybe of potentially  a little bit more challenging experience  absolutely well if you guys want to hear  more about the division to our full  review is on the way so stay tuned to  game spot and check out the rest of our  coverage

